<h2 class="design">The Passing of Marcel Marceau</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">Describing the beauty of silence </h4>

<p>

I've always found mime a chuckle, but when I heard that Marcel Marceau had died I wondered how someone would find words to describe what he did without them. I thought <a href="http://hosted.ap.org/dynamic/stories/O/OBIT_MARCEAU_GENT-?SITE=WIFON&SECTION=HOME&TEMPLATE=DEFAULT">this AP obituary</a> had some beautiful descriptions. The lede for one. Also the description of his routine, "You, Maturity, Old Age, Death."
